  "term": "deception research",
  "definition": "Deception research is the study of lying and the factors linked to it, including how personal characteristics and life experiences relate to deceptive behavior. In this source, it refers especially to examining whether childhood adversity is associated with how often people tell everyday minor lies and more serious lies in adulthood.",
